{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Showbread (lechem panim):</b> that it has faces visible both this way and that way, toward the sides of the House from here and from there, and one sets its length along the width of the table, and its walls stand upright against the edge of the table — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 25:29). And this is the language of the Mishnah (Menahot 96b): Ben Zoma says, \"lechem panim\" — that it had faces. But all this is according to the one who says (ibid. 94a), \"How do they make it? Like an open box.\" But according to the one who says (ibid.), \"like a dancing ship,\" it is not so. And R. Abraham Ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 25:30) that it is called lechem panim on account of \"before Me always.\" And by way of truth, when you understand the expression \"before Me\" (here), you will understand its name and its secret, for because it is thus, it was placed in the north, for \"the blessing of YHWH, it makes rich\" (Proverbs 10:22), as it is written (Exodus 20:21), \"In every place where I cause My name to be remembered I will come to you and bless you,\" and I already hinted at it (Exodus 3): the wisdom of the Menorah — its goblets, its knobs, and its blossoms — \"from where shall it be found?\" And it is hidden exceedingly (cf. Job 28:20–21). But its being hammered from six branches going out from the seventh, and upon them \"the lamp of Elohim\" (Exodus 25:37), all of them giving light \"toward the side of its face\" (ibid.) — all this you will be able to understand from our words that we wrote in another place, and this is their saying (Menahot 29a), that Moses was stymied by the Menorah:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "In the kabbalistic passage, the phrase 'נר אלהים' is drawn from 1 Samuel 3:3 rather than Exodus 25:37; Ramban appears to weave the biblical locution into his reading of the Menorah passage, so it is left as a Hebrew phrase within the argument."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:16:32.688197168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}